-START_SCRIPT
-PROG_NAME
	Headline Harry and the Great Paper Race
-BYTES_NEEDED
	3600000
-SPEAKER_MINVAL
	30
-DEF_SORC_PATH
	B:\
-DEF_DEST_PATH
	C:\HH
-CPYRGHT_MSG
	Copyright (c) 1991 by Davidson & Associates, Inc.
-SET_SWAP_PRMPT
	In order to conserve space, some Harry files may be 
	deleted from your hard disk and new Harry files copied
	from the original disks.  
-INS_OPEN_MSG
	Hard Disk Install Version 1.0 written by Frank Sasaki and
	Phil Van Duyne.
	This program will copy all of the files needed to install 
	Headline Harry onto your system.  Headline Harry requires
	different amounts of disk space depending on the configuration
	of your system.  Selecting Internal Speaker for slower machines
	can save 1,000,000 bytes of Hard Disk space. Normal Headline 
	Harry installation requires about 3,600,000 bytes of available 
	disk space. Press Enter to continue, press Esc to abort.
-SET_OPEN_MSG
	This program will allow you to change the type of video mode
	and sound card that Headline Harry will use. 
-UN_OPEN_MSG
	Uninstall will delete any files that were previously installed.
-SORC_PRMPT
	Enter the SOURCE drive letter ( e.g. B:\ ).
-DEST_PRMPT
	Enter the DESTINATION drive and path.
-DISK_PRMPT
	Please insert the disk labeled 
-INS_END_MSG
	Headline Harry is now installed on your system.
-SET_END_MSG
	Headline Harry setup is complete.
-UN_END_MSG
	Headline Harry uninstall completed.
-SET_VID_PRMPT
	Select one of the following video modes
	by using the up-arrow and down-arrow keys.
	If you are unsure of the Video mode just hit enter.		
	
	   VGA (Video Graphics Array)
	   MCGA (MultiColor Graphics Array)
	   EGA (Enhanced Graphics Adapter)
	   CGA (Color Graphics Adapter)
	   BWCGA (Black and White Color Graphics Adapter)
	   TGA (Tandy Graphics Array)
	   HERCULES (Hercules Graphics Card)
-SET_SND_PRMPT
	Select one of the following sound cards.
	If you are unsure of the Sound card just hit enter.		
	
	   Internal Speaker on a slower machine
	   SoundBlaster
	   Adlib
	   IBM Ps-1 Speech accessory
	   Tandy SL,TL or XL2500
	   Internal Speaker on a 10 megahertz AT or better
-SET_PORT_PRMPT
	Select the port that your SoundBlaster card
	is installed to.  If you are not certain
	which one is correct, press ENTER to accept
	the detected port.
	
	   Port 210
	   Port 220
	   Port 230
	   Port 240
	   Port 250
	   Port 260
